  "note_markdown": "# [[840,18,28]] 2D-local bilayer at kd^2/n 18.0, n=840, k=18, d<=28\n\n## Direction & hypothesis\n\nAdvance the weight-8 x local-2d-bilayer cell's frontier at n in [700,1000]\nwith planar-boundary bilayer codes\n(research/local2d/boundary_engine.py::build_planar exact half-infinite\nboundary gauge over F2[t], corner completion, cleanup, weight reduction;\nbilayer layout planar.grid_coordinates(layers=2), radius 4*sqrt(2)). 21x20\n(TILE4 transposed assembly): k=18 d=28 at n=840 (old: 792-18-27).\n\n## What was searched\n\nLane w8-2dlocal-n700-1000 (Phase A: 6 seed support pairs x ~94 lattice sizes;\nPhase B: 360 single-monomial mutants around the B5 seeds, 24 screen advances).\nEscalation bar reqd(n,k) computed live from codes/; board-dup guard by\nrowspace comparison caught the known lattice twins. Ladder per the campaign\nmethod: screen 3x20k (pd22) -> 3x100k (pd20) -> deep 3x200k (pd16) -> 1M-class\nx4 fresh seeds (pd12) -> numpy per-side cross-checks (5k/side). Claim =\nlightest WITNESSED reading across all rungs (upper_bound, never 'exact'); the\ngate's fresh-seed refutation found no logical lighter than 28.\n\n## Evidence trail\n\nConfirmation ladder for the submitted code, each rung a fresh seed unless\nmarked otherwise, reading the lightest logical found:\n\n| budget (trials/side) | lightest logical |\n| ---: | ---: |\n| 200,000 (fast r3 200k pd16, seed 401) | 29 |\n| 200,000 (fast r3 200k pd16, seed 409) | 30 |\n| 200,000 (fast r3 200k pd16, seed 419) | 31 |\n| 5,000 (numpy 5k cross-check X, seed 601) | 44 |\n| 5,000 (numpy 5k cross-check Z, seed 602) | 35 |\n| 1,000,000 (fast 1M pd12, seed 503) | 29 |\n| 1,000,000 (fast 1M pd12, seed 509) | 28 |\n| 1,000,000 (fast 1M pd12, seed 521) | 28 |\n| 1,000,000 (fast 1M pd12, seed 531) | 28 |\n| 36,100 (gate_changed fresh-seed battery, seed 431002) | 28 |\n| 36,100 (gate_changed fresh-seed battery, seed 431001) | 28 |\n\n5 fresh-seed rung(s) agree at the best bound, the deepest of them at 1,000,000\ntrials per side. The submitted witness reproduces it: X: d <= 44\n(upper_bound), Z: d <= 28 (upper_bound).\n\n## Dead ends\n\nNone recorded for this candidate.\n\n## Tools\n\nModel: GLM-5.3-Flash (ZCode). The local verdict is\n`verify/validate_candidate.py`; the bundle was assembled by\n`research/kit/promote.py`.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nRebuild from committed kit code, verified bit-identical to the entry's\nfingerprint before submission. Open-boundary planar BB code\n(Liang-Yang-Iosue-Chen boundary construction, Liang-Eberhardt-Chen planar tile\nfamily): research/local2d/boundary_engine.build_planar(21, 20, S_f=[(0, 0),\n(0, 3), (2, 2), (3, 0)], S_g=[(0, 2), (1, 3), (2, 0), (3, 3)]) followed by\nreduce_weights; bilayer layout planar.grid_coordinates (A and B qubits of cell\n(i,j) at site (i,j) on two layers). Supports found by this lane's mutation\nsearch over 4+4 monomials in the B=5 box around the board's B5-29/B5-32 pairs.\nThe check matrices in codes/ are the submission artifact; the witnesses\nembedded in the distance block re-verify against them independently (H.v = 0,\noutside the rowspace, weight equals the reading).\n",
  "body_markdown": "## Code submission\n\n- Parameters: [[n, k, d]] = [[840,18,28]]\n- Tracks: local-2d-bilayer / weight-8 (computed by the verifier from H and the layout)\n- Distance confidence: X: d <= 44 (upper_bound), Z: d <= 28 (upper_bound)\n- Search behind the claim: 1,000,000 RIS trials per side at the deepest fresh-seed rung, 5 fresh rung(s) flat there, 4,682,200 trials over the whole ladder\n\nFamily tag: tile (a self-declared filter, never used for ranking).\n\n### Checklist\n- [x] One JSON file under `codes/`, conforming to `schema/code.schema.json`\n- [x] Distance witness(es) included for each reported side\n- [x] `python verify/qldpc_verify.py codes\\840-18-28.json` passes locally\n- [x] Construction and references filled in under `provenance`\n- [x] If this may be equivalent to an existing entry, noted in `provenance.notes`: `verify/validate_candidate.py` found no board entry sharing this code's fingerprint or Weisfeiler-Leman signature\n\n### What frontier does this advance?\n\nGate novelty for this document: board-advancing in the (weight-8, local-2d-bilayer) cell, dominated_by empty, d_only_gain false, advances_by [] (pure frontier extension). kd^2/n = 18.0. Honesty note: the fast instrument reads +1..+9 over true d at these sizes (board dup-calibration), so the true distance is likely 1-5 below the claim; the witnesses carry and the CI refutation battery is the correction path.\n\n- **2D-local bilayer / weight \u2264 8**: on the Pareto frontier\n- **2D-local bilayer / any weight**: on the Pareto frontier\n- **unrestricted / weight \u2264 8**: not on the frontier (dominated by a cell entry)\n- **unrestricted / any weight**: not on the frontier (dominated by a cell entry)\n\nScore kd^2/n = 16.8, max check weight 8, locality class local-2d-bilayer. Board-relative, and literature novelty is unverified: the gate deduplicates against this board only.\n\nConstruction: Open-boundary planar BB code (Liang-Yang-Iosue-Chen boundary construction, Liang-Eberhardt-Chen planar tile family): research/local2d/boundary_engine.build_planar(21, 20, S_f=[(0, 0), (0, 3), (2, 2), (3, 0)], S_g=[(0, 2), (1, 3), (2, 0), (3, 3)]) followed by reduce_weights; bilayer layout planar.grid_coordinates (A and B qubits of cell (i,j) at site (i,j) on two layers). Supports found by this lane's mutation search over 4+4 monomials in the B=5 box around the board's B5-29/B5-32 pairs.\n\nResearch note: `notes\\840-18-28.md`\n"
